@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Hotbar: Figma to Roblox notes
+
+Source: `design/figma/hotbar.json` (Figma file "Block Builder - UI", version 2208815566419836712).
+Node `31:100` is the "HUD / Desktop" frame (1920x1080), node `31:2` the "Hotbar Slot" component
+set (variants Default, Hover, Pressed, Selected; properties Key and Show Key). No screenshot came
+with the export, so the port was checked against the layer boxes in the JSON, not by eye.
+
+The 1920x1080 frame is 1080 tall, the height the project's UI is authored for, so every Figma
+number is used as is (scale 1). Tokens live in `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/Theme.luau`.
+
+## What Roblox can't reproduce exactly
+
+| Design | What the Roblox hotbar uses | Visible difference |
+|---|---|---|
+| Selected Name font: Gilroy ExtraBold (800) | Montserrat ExtraBold, the closest geometric sans Roblox ships | Different letter shapes; the label's width changes with the font (the design's "Brick" box is 70 px wide) |
+| Selected Name letter spacing -0.5 px | Default spacing: Roblox text has no letter spacing setting | Text is about 0.5 px wider per letter |
+| Hotbar layer opacity 80% (the bar and everything in it fade as one picture) | The 80% folded into each layer's own transparency: bar fill, slot fills, swatches, outline, and key text at 0.2; key badge at 0.56 (55% x 80%); top edge at 0.904 (12% x 80%) | Layers now stack: about 4% of the world shows through a slot instead of 20%, and swatches are tinted slightly toward the slot's navy rather than the world. A `CanvasGroup` would match exactly, but it renders the always-visible HUD to a texture and goes soft on scaled screens, so it wasn't used |
+| Hotbar stroke on the top side only (2 px, inside, white 12%), tapering around the 14 px corners | One 2 px inner `UIStroke` around the whole bar, faded out by a vertical `UIGradient` over the top 14 px | Close to the design's taper; the curve of the fade differs slightly from Figma's stroke taper at the corners |
+| Slot corner smoothing 0.6 (squircle corners), radius 12 | Plain circular `UICorner` radius 12 | Corners are slightly less smooth where they meet the straight edges; hard to see at 64 px |
+
+Everything else maps directly: fills and alpha, 14/12/8 px corner radii, the 18 px round key
+badge, the 3 px outside gradient outline on the selected slot (`UIStroke` with a `UIGradient`,
+yellow `#FFD25A` to orange `#FF801A`, left to right), the text outline on the block name
+(2 px, black 60%), auto layout padding 10 and gap 8, and the Pressed variant's 60 px body with a
+36 px swatch.
+
+## States the design doesn't show, filled from its tokens
+
+Please review these with the designer:
+
+- **Selected and hovered, or selected and pressed:** the slot takes the Hover or Pressed fill (and
+  the Pressed size) and keeps the gradient outline.
+- **Gamepad focus:** a slot focused with a gamepad takes the Hover look.
+- **Pressed on touch:** the Pressed look shows while a finger is down on a slot.
+- **Motion:** the file has no prototype transitions, so state changes are instant.
+
+## Other things to know
+
+- **Pressed doesn't move the neighbors.** Each slot keeps its 64 px cell; only the body inside
+  shrinks to 60 px, so the row never reflows.
+- **Swatch colors come from the game.** The design shows Brick's color in every slot as a
+  placeholder; each slot shows its block's color from `BlockTypes`. See-through blocks (Window,
+  Ice) still show a solid swatch, as before.
+- **Desktop only.** There is no phone or tablet frame. The bar is 732 px wide at scale 1 (the old
+  one was 630), which is wider than many landscape phones and can sit under the touch thumbstick
+  and jump button. A phone layout needs a design.
+
+## Measured boxes to compare (1920x1080, scale 1)
+
+| Element | Figma box (x, y, w, h) |
+|---|---|
+| Selected Name | centered on x 960, y 936, h 28 |
+| Hotbar bar | 594, 972, 732, 84 |
+| Slot 1 | 604, 982, 64, 64 (next slots every 72 px) |
+| Slot 1 swatch | 616, 994, 40, 40 |
+| Slot 1 key badge | 608, 986, 18, 18 |
